# BuildKit prefers this file over .dockerignore when building with --file Dockerfile.cli, so it fully
# replaces those rules rather than adding to them. Keeping the CLI context separate means neither image
# accumulates re-includes for the other's build inputs.
#
# Like .dockerignore, this excludes everything and re-includes only what the Dockerfile copies. Each
# parent directory has to be re-included before its children become reachable.
**
!Dockerfile.cli
!artifacts/
!artifacts/docker/
!artifacts/docker/cli/
!artifacts/docker/cli/**
!docker/
!docker/cli-workdir/
!docker/cli-workdir/**
